    <!-- Understanding American Odds -->
    <div data-controller="collapsible" class="bg-gray-100 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg">
      <div class="flex items-center p-4 sm:p-5 cursor-pointer select-none hover:bg-gray-200 transition-colors duration-200"
           data-action="click->collapsible#toggle">
        <span class="inline-block mr-3 sm:mr-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 transition-transform duration-300"
              data-collapsible-target="arrow"
              aria-expanded="false">▶</span>
        <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 m-0">How do American odds work?</h3>
      </div>
      <div data-collapsible-target="content" class="border-t border-gray-300 p-4 sm:p-5 bg-white rounded-b-lg">
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          American odds show how much you can win relative to $100:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 mt-3 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Negative odds (e.g., -150)</strong> - The amount you must bet to win $100. A -150 bet means wagering $150 to win $100 profit. This indicates the favorite.</li>
          <li><strong>Positive odds (e.g., +130)</strong> - The amount you win on a $100 bet. A +130 bet means winning $130 profit on a $100 wager. This indicates the underdog.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3">
          <strong>Example:</strong> If you bet $50 on a team at +200 odds and win, you profit $100 (plus your $50 stake back).
          If you bet $50 on a team at -200 odds and win, you profit $25 (plus your $50 stake back).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What happens to my bets? -->
    <div data-controller="collapsible" class="bg-gray-100 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg">
      <div class="flex items-center p-4 sm:p-5 cursor-pointer select-none hover:bg-gray-200 transition-colors duration-200"
           data-action="click->collapsible#toggle">
        <span class="inline-block mr-3 sm:mr-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 transition-transform duration-300"
              data-collapsible-target="arrow"
              aria-expanded="false">▶</span>
        <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 m-0">What happens after I place a bet?</h3>
      </div>
      <div data-collapsible-target="content" class="border-t border-gray-300 p-4 sm:p-5 bg-white rounded-b-lg">
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          After placing a bet, it moves through these stages:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 mt-3 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Pending</strong> - Your bet is waiting for the game to complete. You can cancel pending bets before the game starts.</li>
          <li><strong>Won</strong> - Your bet was successful! Your winnings are added to your bankroll.</li>
          <li><strong>Lost</strong> - Your bet didn't hit. The wagered amount is forfeited.</li>
          <li><strong>Push</strong> - The result was exactly on the line (tie). Your original stake is returned.</li>
          <li><strong>Canceled</strong> - You canceled the bet before the game started, and your stake was refunded.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3">
          View all your bets and their statuses on the "My Bets" page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What is the house vig? -->
    <div data-controller="collapsible" class="bg-gray-100 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg">
      <div class="flex items-center p-4 sm:p-5 cursor-pointer select-none hover:bg-gray-200 transition-colors duration-200"
           data-action="click->collapsible#toggle">
        <span class="inline-block mr-3 sm:mr-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 transition-transform duration-300"
              data-collapsible-target="arrow"
              aria-expanded="false">▶</span>
        <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 m-0">What is the house vig (vigorish)?</h3>
      </div>
      <div data-collapsible-target="content" class="border-t border-gray-300 p-4 sm:p-5 bg-white rounded-b-lg">
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          The <strong>vig</strong> (short for vigorish, also called "juice") is the commission the house takes on every bet.
          It's how sportsbooks guarantee profit regardless of outcomes.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3">
          <strong>How it works:</strong> On a standard spread bet, both sides are typically -110. This means you bet $110 to win $100.
          If two people bet opposite sides of the same game, one wins $100 while the other loses $110.
          The sportsbook keeps the $10 difference - that's the vig.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-3">
          We track the house vig publicly so you can see exactly how much of the betting pool goes to "the house" over time.
          This transparency helps you understand why consistent winning requires more than just picking 50% of your bets correctly.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
            <strong>Did you know?</strong> To break even with standard -110 odds, you need to win approximately 52.4% of your bets.
            The vig is why long-term profitable sports betting is so challenging!
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

